{"nodes": [{"id": "card___hostbrands", "label": "window.__hostBrands (hostname white-label map)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:21-33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_shade", "label": "shade (head IIFE colour shader)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:47-56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_hostname_white_label", "label": "Hostname-aware white-label bootstrap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:19-94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On a custom domain (card.washhub.it) the brand is applied synchronously in <head> before CSS loads: document.title, manifest (manifest-washhub.json), theme-color, apple-touch-icon/title and an injected <style> for body/.card-app gradient. Done this early so iOS 'Add to Home Screen' captures the merchant branding and there is no FidelAI flash. A second body IIFE fills merchant name/logo on DOMContentLoaded. Merchant Firestore ID is also resolved from the hostname (HOSTNAME_MERCHANTS) so NFC/short links need no ?m= param."}, {"id": "card_firebaseconfig", "label": "firebaseConfig (card)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:224", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_hostname_merchants", "label": "HOSTNAME_MERCHANTS", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:236", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_api_base", "label": "API_BASE (europe-west1 Cloud Functions)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:243", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_storage_key", "label": "STORAGE_KEY (fidelai_customer_<merchantId>)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:244", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_getstoredcustomerid", "label": "getStoredCustomerId", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:246", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_setstoredcustomerid", "label": "setStoredCustomerId", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:250", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_normalizephoneclient", "label": "normalizePhoneClient", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:255", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strips non-digits and a leading '39' country code so the phone becomes the canonical customer document ID; must stay in sync with server-side normalisation in selfActivateCard."}, {"id": "card_showactivateview", "label": "showActivateView", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:262", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_setupactivateform", "label": "setupActivateForm", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:271", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_self_activation_flow", "label": "Card self-activation flow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:130-168,262-349", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If no customer id (?c= param or localStorage) or the customer doc has cardAttivata !== true, the activation form is shown instead of the card. Form POSTs {merchant slug, name, phone, email, consentPrivacy, consentSms, consentEmail} to the selfActivateCard Cloud Function (merchant slug from __hostBrands, falling back to Firestore merchantId). Privacy consent is mandatory, SMS/email marketing consents optional (GDPR fix 025a1dc). On success the normalised phone is stored as the customer id in localStorage and the page reloads with ?c=<phone>, so returning visitors on the same device open the card directly. Stale localStorage ids are cleared when the doc is missing/unactivated."}, {"id": "card_loadcard", "label": "loadCard", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:319", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_client_side_reward_sort", "label": "Client-side reward sort (composite index workaround)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:367-372", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rewards query is where('active'==true) only and sorted by pointsCost in JS. The original active+orderBy(pointsCost) needed a Firestore composite index that was never created, so the query failed silently and no rewards appeared on the card (fixed 26/10/2026, commit e531d04). Sorting client-side avoids depending on index deployment."}, {"id": "card_onredeemclick", "label": "onRedeemClick", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:430", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_showredeemmodal", "label": "showRedeemModal", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:452", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_redeem_code_flow", "label": "Redeem code flow (4-digit code, 5-min TTL)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:109-119,430-478", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Customer taps 'Riscatta' -> confirm() -> POST generateRedeemCode {merchant, customerId, rewardId} -> server returns {code, expiresAt, rewardName, pointsCost}. Code is shown full-screen with a live countdown so the cashier can type/read it at the till; points are deducted server-side when the operator confirms the code, not on the card. Closing the modal calls loadCard() to refresh points and history."}, {"id": "card_applybranding", "label": "applyBranding", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:480", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only applies merchant.branding when merchant.plan is in WHITELABEL_PLANS ['pro','business'] - plan gating is enforced on the card side too, not just in the dashboard form. primaryColor is validated as #rrggbb before use; theme-color meta is set to the darkened shade."}, {"id": "card_shadecolor", "label": "shadeColor", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:507", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_setupinstallbanner", "label": "setupInstallBanner", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:518", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PWA install nudge: uses beforeinstallprompt on Android/Chrome, and on iOS Safari (no install API) shows manual 'Share -> Add to Home Screen' instructions after 1.5 s. Hidden in standalone mode and after dismissal (sessionStorage)."}, {"id": "card_getlevel", "label": "getLevel", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:562", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "card_loyalty_levels", "label": "Loyalty levels Bronze/Silver/Gold/Platinum (0/500/1500/5000)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:563-568", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Level thresholds are hard-coded in card.html getLevel and duplicated as static markup in dashboard.html module-loyalty; not configurable per merchant yet. Changing thresholds requires editing both."}, {"id": "card_renderdemo", "label": "renderDemo", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:576", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "?demo=true renders static 'Bar Roma / Marco Rossi' data without Firestore; ?brand=custom additionally runs applyBranding with a fake Pro merchant 'Caffe Aurora' to show the white-label card on the landing page."}, {"id": "card_service_worker_registration", "label": "Service worker registration (sw.js)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:613-619", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "card_hostname_white_label", "target": "card___hostbrands", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:35,81", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "card_hostname_white_label", "target": "card_shade", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:57-58", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "card_hostname_white_label", "target": "card_hostname_merchants", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:240", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "card_shade", "target": "card_shadecolor", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "card.html", "source_location": "card.html:47,507", "